{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788029806909781909,"compiled_state":{"alias":"earthborn-statuelike-boutu","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"429a29513c4640c963ef3bd732e18e3d59cc390f9609eea95b050bade348f37c","event_uuid":"beb7b0fc-a2fb-4377-a92f-c21778902465","position":{"commit_sha":"2ecbc942021ef88dab7cd10e0a800dc397769c12","position":"1788026443688325591-beb7b0fc-a2fb-4377-a92f-c21778902465"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0b037468018fc74ed0c13b7dd70ada4d24c053bc1d1a8e22b873b129b77577ab","event_uuid":"7a110fb0-0528-4bef-a7bb-93bb84e3e7be","position":{"commit_sha":"4bc494b2cd86913b0ec72688f300e372fcd27ba6","position":"1788026490561786689-7a110fb0-0528-4bef-a7bb-93bb84e3e7be"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d123d290fcfb4b2576e8ff4e87576b5c707eb455cfda238df8dcaab072571c61","event_uuid":"71907fb3-eae7-4347-803b-eb45875e621c","position":{"commit_sha":"ecaeecec649686b4a589a09394a04843d3708a3a","position":"1788026584390478653-71907fb3-eae7-4347-803b-eb45875e621c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1c7258e98ab3c51649bad53138822ac58ba54180f12ba93612e1057aac3ce0b5","event_uuid":"96b21126-c446-4d3f-a66f-e7fede867c78","position":{"commit_sha":"6705b1482432ddc433287ff14ae4cd04e139da10","position":"1788026776230835898-96b21126-c446-4d3f-a66f-e7fede867c78"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788026443688325591,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7a110fb0-0528-4bef-a7bb-93bb84e3e7be","relation":"blocks","target_id":"3f27-cb3c-8023-4f57"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nImplement the contract decided by the preceding architecture story without changing the production write route yet. The key deliverable is sufficient deterministic parity evidence to make the later cutover/deletion safe within this epic.\n\nExisting useful assets include the real store-copy scrub/isolation fixtures, canonical serialization, route census, verified Cloud/DC fakes, and comprehensive mutation tests. Reuse them rather than creating a parallel reconciler harness.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduce the approved direction/action payload union and thread it through planner and coordinator boundaries up to a side-effect-free adapter projection seam.\n- Build a versioned corpus from deterministic synthetic tickets plus a scrubbed representative store snapshot. Include edge and failure shapes, not credentials or live bindings.\n- Drive legacy and typed planning/serialization over identical observations. Capture canonical normalized intent/outcome traces without invoking either writer.\n- Compare ordering, fields, identity scopes, diagnostics, follow-ons, suppression, retry dispositions, and modeled final state.\n- Run this oracle in default portable CI with no Jira, Docker, external service, or CI-provider dependency.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — typed payloads and the effect-free trace projection.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — portable replay and verified adapter contracts.\n- `tests/fixtures/` — versioned synthetic/scrubbed corpus with no credentials or live bindings.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: representative inbound and outbound mutations produce matching normalized legacy/typed traces and modeled state. Edge/failure paths: malformed payloads, ambiguous commits, exhaustion, suppression, follow-ons, and cross-project routes either match or produce an approved named delta. Effect spies fail if the shadow path reaches Jira, the ticket store, a subprocess, clock sleep, or network.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Planners and coordinator use named payload types for every supported direction/action pair; construction rejects missing, extra critical, or wrong-action fields before effects.\n- [ ] The shadow comparator executes no Jira transport or ticket-store write, proven with failing spies on every effect seam.\n- [ ] The corpus covers create/update/delete/probe/conflict, inbound-only actions, links/comments/labels/status/parent/assignee/binding fields, duplicate and malformed inputs, suppression/follow-ons, ambiguous outcomes, retry exhaustion, and multi-project routing.\n- [ ] Replaying the same corpus is deterministic and idempotent; corpus version/provenance and normalization rules are explicit.\n- [ ] Legacy and typed traces have zero unexplained differences. Each intentional delta has a named test, rationale, and approval recorded on the ticket.\n- [ ] Verified-fake Jira Cloud and Data Center adapter contract tests pass without selecting a live backend.\n- [ ] Production continues to use the pre-cutover route in this story, and no temporary bridge is presented as the final architecture.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"Typed payload union and side-effect-free trace projection."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"Portable legacy-versus-typed shadow replay."},{"path":"tests/fixtures/","reason":"Versioned synthetic/scrubbed replay corpus."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","3f27-cb3c-8023-4f57"],["parent","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["reconciler","testing","migration"],"ticket_id":"e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Build typed reconciler payloads and a portable shadow-replay corpus","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["beb7b0fc-a2fb-4377-a92f-c21778902465","7a110fb0-0528-4bef-a7bb-93bb84e3e7be","71907fb3-eae7-4347-803b-eb45875e621c","96b21126-c446-4d3f-a66f-e7fede867c78"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788029806909781909,"uuid":"c38a67d7-5ed4-450e-b7d1-c2157f848cc3"}